(The alt attribute is the text a screen reader announces in place of an image and what a browser shows when the image fails to load. It is) Tj
T* (also the main signal Google Images uses to understand a picture. An <img> with no alt attribute at all is an accessibility failure \(WCAG) Tj
T* (1.1.1\); one with alt="" is valid only when the image is purely decorative.) Tj
