39.6850393700787407 279.2128346456692043 Td
(For every meaningful image, add an alt attribute that describes what the image conveys in context, e.g. <img src="/team/ana.jpg" alt="Ana) Tj
T* (Ruiz, Head of SEO, speaking at a conference">. Keep it concise \(roughly under 125 characters\), don't start with "image of" or "picture of",) Tj
T* (and don't keyword-stuff. For decorative images \(spacers, background flourishes, icons next to text that already says the same thing\) use) Tj
T* (an explicit empty alt="" so assistive tech skips them. In a CMS, fill the "alt text" / "alternative text" field on each media item; in templates,) Tj
T* (make the alt a required field of the image component so new content can't ship without it. For CSS background images that carry) Tj
T* (meaning, move them into <img> so they can have alt text.) Tj
